      "title": "Walsh University Alumni & Career Connections",
      "description": "Office of Alumni & Career Connections SKIP TO PAGE CONTENT Menu Mobile Menu Mobile Site Search Academics Undergraduate Programs Graduate Programs Online & Accelerated Programs Academic Services Experiential Learning Academic and Community Engagement Centers Alumni and Career Connections Office of the Registrar Academic Calendar Class Schedules Admission & Aid First-Time Students WU Promise Grant Transfer Students International Students Military & Veteran Students Service to Scholars Discount Program First Generation Students Graduate Students Virtual Tour Financial Aid College Credit Plus Online & Accelerated Students Athletics Campus Life Office of Student Experience Campus Ministry Cavs Cor Cordium Activities & Organizations Visual & Performing Arts Housing & Dining Counseling & Health Services Campus Safety Online & Accelerated Undergraduate Programs Graduate Programs Certificates Licensures & Endorsements Skilled Workforce Training Request Info Library Give Visit Apply MyWalsh Search the Website Search Our Website Submit Walsh University Alumni & Career Connections Share on Facebook Share on Twitter/X Share on LinkedIn Email this page: Walsh University Alumni & Career Connections Print this page The Office of Alumni & Career Connections helps students bridge their college experience into their career. Students who connect with us early gain valuable advantages including stronger resumes, expanded professional networks, increased awareness of internship and career opportunities and greater confidence in navigating the job search process. We help students create strong Handshake and LinkedIn profiles, practice interviewing, and develop their personal brand and confidence so they present themselves professionally. Our goal is to help you discover career paths that match your interests, skills, and values—and give you the tools to succeed in today’s job market. And we won’t do it alone. Our strong alumni network connects you with professionals from various fields who offer real-world advice, mentorship, and industry insights. We encourage you to attend our career fairs, networking events and employer panel presentations to meet employers, explore internships, and even secure job opportunities before you graduate. Follow us on social media for career tips, upcoming events, and alumni success stories. Launch your future by connecting with us on Handshake (#1 site for college students to find professional opportunities) to schedule an appointment with us and to connect with employers across Northeast Ohio and beyond. Alumni Resources Find out more ways to connect with fellow alumni, stay engaged with Walsh, and how you can make a difference on campus and in the community. Learn More Career Connections Resources Connect with alumni, meet employers, and explore careers that match your interests. We’re here to help you build confidence and take steps toward your goals. Connect with us early so you can take advantage of everything available to you and be ready for the workforce. Learn More Stephanie Koontz\n\t\t\t\t- Assistant Vice President of Alumni and Career Connections Phone: 330.244.4943 Email: skoontz@walsh.edu Office: Global Learning Center, Office 133 Annette Bernard\n\t\t\t\t- Director of Alumni and Career Connections Phone: 330.490.7380 Email: abernard@walsh.edu Office: Global Learning Center, Office 134 Robin Clark\n\t\t\t\t- Professional Development Coordinator Phone: 330-244-4974 Email: rclark@walsh.edu Office: Global Learning Center, Office 135 About Walsh Accreditation Bookstore Campus Map Campus Safety & Security Conferences & Events Consumer Information Emergency Information Employment Maintenance Request Mass Times Non-Discrimination Policy Privacy Policy Web Accessibility 2020 East Maple Street North Canton, Ohio 44720 800.362.9846 Toll-free 330.490.7090 Local Follow us on: Like us on Facebook Follow us on X Connect with us on LinkedIn Watch us on YouTube See us on Instagram Walsh University 